{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:0.2"], "en": "Tikanipāta,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:0.3"], "en": "Kumbhavagga", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:0.4", "PA_ja_296:1.1"], "en": "6. The Samudda Jātaka “Who is this that runs all around within the salt waters?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:1.2"], "en": "Who is this that runs about in the midst of the ocean?”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:1.3"], "en": "He wards off fish and crocodiles,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:1.4"], "en": "yet he is distressed by the waves.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:2.1"], "en": "“The bird Anantapāyī— ”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:2.2"], "en": "“Unsatisfied,” he said,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:2.3"], "en": "“I have heard of the directions; I wish to drink the ocean,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:2.4"], "en": "the sea, the lord of rivers.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:3.1", "PA_ja_296:3.2"], "en": "“Thus this great ocean both diminishes and fills;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:3.3"], "en": "its depth cannot be measured.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:3.4"], "en": "“Indeed, the ocean is undrinkable.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_296:4.1"], "en": "Thus ends the sixth Jātaka, the Samudda-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
]
